The city clerk, after receiving input from council members, staff, the city attorney, and members of the public, shall set a proposed order of agenda items to be submitted for council approval at the beginning of each meeting of the mayor and council. All department heads, staff, councilmembers and citizens desiring to bring business or general public comment topics, other than for a public hearing, before the mayor and council shall notify the city clerk by 1:00 p.m. on the Thursday prior to the Monday preceding the upcoming meeting and send all supporting documentation to the city clerk. The meeting agenda, and supplements thereto, will be available to the general public and the mayor and council the Monday preceding the upcoming meeting, and a notice containing such information will be posted and maintained in a conspicuous place available to the public at the regular meeting place of the agency and on any city website. The agenda shall list all items to be considered at a particular meeting. Any item received after the deadline by the city clerk will be held over until the next meeting. Any public comment received by any staff member after the agenda deadline shall be immediately forwarded to the mayor and city council. For specially called meetings, other than the regularly scheduled monthly meeting, the agenda shall consist only of the item or items specifically indicated as the purpose of the called meeting in accordance with the Open Meetings Act. Failure to include on the agenda an item does not take away the mayor and city council's ability to amend the agenda in their work session or regular agenda. The permanent agenda format shall be the following:
(1) Call to order;
(2) Pledge of allegiance;
(3) Roll call;
(4) Approval of minutes of previous meetings;
(5) Approval of order of agenda items;
(6) Identify actionable items for public comment as they arise and before the vote;
(7) Consent agenda;
(8) Zoning hearings on second Mondays, to come after other business on fourth Mondays. Zoning hearings shall only occur when they are scheduled to come before mayor and council;
(9) Legal matters;
(10) Unfinished business;
(11) New business;
(12) Public comments;
(13) Adjournment.
(Amd. of 12-11-2006(2), § 2; Amd. of 8-13-2012(1), § 1(Exh. A); Amd. of 5-12-2014(3), § 1; Amd. of 8-11-14, § 1; Ord. of 04-08-2024(1), § 1)

