(3) Nonalcoholic beverages commonly used to dilute distilled spirits;
(4) Tobacco products;
(5) Ice, to be sold in sealed containers only and not to be opened on the premises;
(6) Paper, styrofoam or plastic cups; and
(7) Distilled spirits (if licensed for such).
Beverages containing no alcohol and commonly used to dilute distilled spirits may be dispensed through the use of vending machines, but no alcohol shall be dispensed through such vending machines.
(d) No licensee shall keep any alcohol in any bonded or other type warehouse in the city, nor enter into any type of arrangement whereby alcohol is stored by any wholesaler. A licensee shall keep no inventory or stock of alcohol at any place except licensed place of business, and within licensed place of business, storage space for distilled spirits shall be immediately adjacent to the distilled spirits display area.
(Amd. of 11-13-2023, § 1)
